course: dictionary
lesson: 7119
title: Peeling: from fruit to paint
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Peeling comes from the verb «peel», which means to take the skin or outer layer off something. The -ing form, peeling, shows that the action is happening now: «Ravi is peeling potatoes» means he is taking the skins off the potatoes at this moment.
explain: Peeling can also describe something whose outer layer is coming off in thin strips or flakes, like «peeling paint» on an old gate or «my skin is peeling» after sunburn. The clue words tell you which meaning fits: a kitchen means food, while an old door or a wall means paint.
explain: Peelings is a noun, usually in the plural. Peelings are the bits of skin you have taken off fruit or vegetables. In «in compost and in soil they break down peelings, dead leaves and dead animals», peelings are things that bacteria and fungi break down, just like leaves.
fact: Peel is the verb; peeling is its -ing form, as in «peeling potatoes».
fact: «Peeling paint» means paint coming off in thin flakes, often on an old, uncared-for house.
fact: «Potato peelings» are the skins you have taken off potatoes.
fact: «Peeling off» means coming away in strips or flakes.
fact: In «Bacteria and fungi are decomposers: in compost and in soil they break down peelings, dead leaves and dead animals», peelings are food scraps that tiny living things break down.
exercise: «Ravi is peeling potatoes for tea.» What is Ravi doing? | Washing his hands | Buying new potatoes | Cooking them in a pan | *Taking the skins off the potatoes
exercise: «The paint on the old gate was peeling.» What is peeling? | A gate that has been painted bright red | Wood being sawn into planks | A fresh coat of paint | *Paint coming off in thin flakes
exercise: Which of these are peelings? | A whole bag of oranges | A glass of fresh orange juice | The orange itself | *The skins you have taken off an orange
test: «My skin is peeling after the sunburn.» What does peeling mean here? | Turning into a hard shell | Getting thicker and redder | *Coming off in thin flakes | Being washed clean in cold water
test: In «in compost and in soil they break down peelings, dead leaves and dead animals», what do bacteria and fungi break down? | Only sunshine and rain | Only the soil itself | *Peelings, dead leaves and dead animals | Flowers and new seeds
exam: Grandma's kitchen had «peeling wallpaper» and a bin full of potato peelings. What does peeling mean in peeling wallpaper? | *Coming off in flakes or strips | Being tidied up neatly | Covered in water droplets | Freshly pasted and shiny
